      "writtenOn": "2024-05-24T21:15:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "FWIW, the logic `profile_initialized \u003d\u003d UUID_SERVCLASS_AUDIO_SOURCE \u0026\u0026 !is_new_avrcp_enabled()` is always false, because `is_new_avrcp_enabled()` is equivalent to \"is AVRCP Target enabled.\" On builds where UUID_SERVCLASS_AUDIO_SOURCE is true, AVRCP Target is always enabled, so !(TRUE) -\u003e FALSE and \u0026\u0026 FALSE is always false. Hope that makes sense 😊\n\nAs I understand it, avrcp_service.cc actually manages the SDP record.\n\nI really want to remove all this dead code relating to \"old AVRCP,\" but alas there\u0027s other priorities.",
